#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:264
msgid ""
"Create `rust-core/src/prose/tinylang.rs`. The module answers two "
"questions, and they are separate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:267
msgid ""
"**Which nodes carry prose?** An AST walk collects the byte ranges of the "
"text leaves, skipping subtrees that hold code, math or metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:269
msgid ""
"**What is in the space between two of them?** That space is a *gap*, and "
"a single function describes what markup can appear there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:272
msgid ""
"**1. Configuration constants** -- node kinds and command names that "
"control what the walk skips:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:292
msgid ""
"**2. AST walk** -- collect the `text` leaves, then hand the result to "
"`shared::merge_ranges` along with the gap syntax from part 3:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:340
msgid ""
"A \"first labeled child\" lookup—a command's `command_name`, a "
"directive's `type` -- is `shared::child_of_kind`, not a hand-written "
"loop:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:350
msgid "**3. Gap syntax** -- the one function a new language has to write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:352
msgid ""
"A gap is the source between two prose words, and it decides two things: "
"whether those words belong to the same prose block, and which byte ranges"
" the checker must not see. Both come from the same question -- *what "
"token starts here?* -- so the language answers it once, as a "
"`gap::Syntax` function, and `gap::strip` and `gap::exclusions` derive the"
" rest:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:392
msgid "Points worth copying:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:394
msgid ""
"**Return `None` for ordinary text.** Anything the function does not "
"recognize is prose, and the scan advances one character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:396
msgid ""
"**Match on `b[i..]`, not on indices.** The slice pattern carries the "
"bounds check, so there is no `i + 1 < len` to forget. `[b'/', b'/', ..]` "
"needs two bytes present; a lone trailing `/` falls through to `_` on its "
"own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:399
msgid ""
"**Order the arms longest-prefix first.** `$$` before `$`, `//` before a "
"bare marker. The first matching arm wins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:401
msgid "**`end` must be greater than `i`,** or the scan cannot make progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:402
msgid ""
"**Work on bytes.** Every delimiter above is single-byte ASCII, so a byte "
"offset that matches is always a character boundary, and non-ASCII prose "
"passes through untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:406
msgid "The token kind says what the checker should see in that range:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md
msgid "Kind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md
msgid "Stripped to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md
msgid "Use for"
